  "published": "2026-07-30T06:24:55.373Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Changed (breaking)\n- **Single root namespace.** Every public type now lives in `Kippo`. The old per-folder namespaces (`Kippo.Attribute`, `Kippo.Contexs`, `Kippo.Extensions`, `Kippo.Keyboard`, `Kippo.Middleware`, `Kippo.Scenes`, `Kippo.SessionStorage`, `Kippo.Handlers`, `Kippo.Callbacks`, `Kippo.Client`, `Kippo.Routers`, `Kippo.Services`) are gone — a bot that previously needed 7–8 `using` directives now needs `using Kippo;`. `Kippo.Testing` stays separate so `TestBot`/`RecordingBotClient` don't surface in production IntelliSense.\n  Migration: delete every `using Kippo.*;` line and add `using Kippo;` (or nothing at all — see below).\n- **Zero-using bots.** The package now ships `buildTransitive/Kippo.targets`, which registers `global using Kippo;` plus `Telegram.Bot`, `Telegram.Bot.Types`, `Telegram.Bot.Types.Enums` and `Telegram.Bot.Types.ReplyMarkups` in consuming projects that have `ImplicitUsings` enabled. Opt out with `<KippoImplicitUsings>false</KippoImplicitUsings>`, or keep only the Kippo using with `<KippoImplicitTelegramUsings>false</KippoImplicitTelegramUsings>`.\n- Infrastructure types that were never meant to be constructed by hand are now `internal`: `CommandRouter`, `BotUpdateHandlerAdapter`, `BotBackgroundService`, `WebhookBootstrapService`, `ThrottlingBotClient`. Flood control is still configured through `AddKippo(..., configureFloodControl: ...)`; a custom `ITelegramBotClient` registered before `AddKippo` is still honored.\n- `ServiceCollectionExtension` renamed to `ServiceCollectionExtensions` (the `AddKippo` extension method itself is unchanged).\n- `Context.Session` is no longer nullable, so `context.Session.Set(...)` no longer trips `CS8604` in nullable-enabled projects. It throws a directed `InvalidOperationException` (instead of a `NullReferenceException`) when the session middleware isn't registered; use the new `Context.HasSession` when the middleware is optional in your setup.\n\n### Internal\n- Source layout reorganized to mirror the API surface: `Attributes/`, `Contexts/` (was the misspelled `Contexs/`), `Sessions/`, `Keyboards/`, `Configuration/`, and a new `Internal/` folder for non-public plumbing. Folders are organizational only — they no longer affect namespaces.",
